cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Sightline: terrain-based visibility planning for Mars EVA"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tyagi
    given-names: Rashi
date-released: 2026-11-15
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Predicts what a walking astronaut can see along a planned Mars EVA route
  (habitat, rover, partner, landmarks) from a digital elevation model, and flags
  low-sun and hidden-ground conditions. Built for the NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026.
keywords: [Mars, EVA, visibility, viewshed, digital elevation model, Gale Crater]
